      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Maple Leafs are being remade in real time, and the loudest move came at the draft table: <strong>Toronto landed Gavin McKenna first overall</strong>, a franchise-altering swing that instantly changes the conversation around its future. With the club finishing 8th in the Atlantic at 78 points, the mandate is plain - get younger, cheaper and sturdier fast. Bruce Boudreau's warning about the defence hanging over the team is no idle jab; it points straight at a blue line that still looks too old for a league that keeps getting faster. Mitch Marner's exit only sharpens the pressure on the front office to replace skill without bloating the cap. The Marlies quietly added structure with Chris Bourque's promotion, but the big question sits upstairs. <strong>What Toronto does next on defence - and whether it finds one more impact scorer - will decide whether McKenna arrives to a reset or a retool.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 23, 2026"
      },
