        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The slide has become a crater - and the Blue Jays are still digging. <strong>Toronto's 4-2 loss to Tampa Bay on Wednesday was its fourth straight defeat</strong>, leaving a 46-56 club in fifth place in the AL East, 13.5 games back, with the season-series beatdown already sealed. The offense keeps sputtering in public: three losses to the Rays in three nights, 12-2, 7-1 and now 4-2, with Alejandro Kirk's third homer of the year only briefly slowing the damage. That is six runs in the past five games - a brutal diet for any lineup, let alone one trying to stop a nosedive before the deadline. <strong>Now the Jays turn right back around for Thursday's 3:07 p.m. ET rematch with the Rays</strong>, and they badly need a pulse.",
